# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; this file is not,
# so never put a real value here.
#
# Every variable is listed with what happens when it is missing in
# docs/tech-stack.md, and set up step by step in DEPLOY.md. Devnet only: there
# is no network or mode variable, and there must not be one — the cluster is a
# constant in the generated lib/deployments.ts.
#
# The minimum for a local run: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for the chat, plus
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID, PRIVY_APP_SECRET and SOLANA_RESOLVER_SECRET for
# login, faucet and checkout. Everything else has a local default.

# ---- the agent -------------------------------------------------------------
# console.anthropic.com -> API keys. Server-side only: it is what /api/chat
# uses to run the shopping agent.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional, and it changes the provider. If OPENAI_API_KEY is set, the agent
# runs on OpenAI instead of Anthropic (lib/agent/providers/openai.ts) — the
# choice follows which key exists. Leave it empty unless you mean that.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1

# ---- sign-in: Privy --------------------------------------------------------
# dashboard.privy.io -> your app -> Settings. The app id is public and ships in
# the browser bundle; the secret never does.
#
# The dashboard needs: email and Google login, Solana embedded wallets created
# on login for all users, and allowed origins http://localhost:3124 plus your
# deployed domain (DEPLOY.md 1.2). Gas sponsorship is not needed: the resolver
# pays the `open` fee (SOLANA_RESOLVER_SECRET).
#
# Without the app id the wallet button renders disabled and nobody can sign in
# or pay; chat still works, with the guest limit.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=

# Required for login. The access token is verified against Privy's public
# JWKS, but the user's linked Solana wallet is read from Privy's API with this
# secret — without it /api/session/login answers 401 to everyone.
PRIVY_APP_SECRET=

# Required in production. Signs the httpOnly `chg_user` cookie issued after a
# verified Privy login, which lifts the three-free-turn guest limit on
# /api/chat and is what the faucet and checkout routes authorize against.
#
# Production uses this and nothing else: unset, login answers 503. Locally it
# falls back to TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY, then to a public dev constant — which is
# what scripts/devnet-e2e.mts signs with, so leave both unset to run it.
# Any long random string, different from the Turnstile secret:
#
#     openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Rotating it signs everyone out, which costs them one email code.
# CHG_SESSION_SECRET=

# ---- Solana ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The resolver keypair: signs settle and refund on the escrow, pays the fee for
# every shopper's `open`, and mints the faucet's devnet USDC (it is the mint
# authority). Keep it topped up with devnet SOL. Either the 64-number JSON
# array solana-keygen writes, or its base58 form:
#
#     cat ~/.config/solana/changuito/resolver.json
#
# Its public key must equal the resolver in lib/deployments.ts; a different
# key is refused at the first call rather than signing. Read at call time, so a
# build without it succeeds — the faucet then answers 503, and checkout cannot
# settle or refund. Server-side only: never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never logged.
SOLANA_RESOLVER_SECRET=

# Optional. Server and browser RPC endpoints. Both default to the public
# https://api.devnet.solana.com, which rate-limits; use a dedicated devnet RPC
# on a public deployment.
# SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com

# ---- the checkout sandbox --------------------------------------------------
# The browser agent that walks Día's checkout (services/sandbox, on Railway).
# SANDBOX_TOKEN must equal the service's own SANDBOX_TOKEN.
#
# Unset locally, an in-process mock plays the phases (about 20 seconds to the
# payment step) and the order settles. Unset in production, checkout is off and
# every locked order is refunded at the first status poll — unless
# SANDBOX_MOCK=1, which lets a production build run on the mock for a demo.
# SANDBOX_URL=https://<your-service>.up.railway.app
# SANDBOX_TOKEN=
# SANDBOX_MOCK=1

# Makes the mock fail at checkout, so the order is refunded. For testing the
# refund path.
# SANDBOX_MOCK_FAIL=1

# ---- the human gate --------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare dashboard -> Turnstile -> add a site. The site key is rendered
# into the widget; the secret verifies the token server-side.
#
# The secret alone decides the gate: set it and the gate enforces, leave it
# unset in production and the gate is "closed" — middleware.ts then answers 403
# `solo_humanos` on every /api/* route except /api/human, so chat, login,
# faucet and checkout are all dead. That is deliberate: an open agent
# endpoint on a public URL bills someone's Anthropic key, and failing shut is
# the only safe way to be misconfigured.
#
# The site key deliberately does not affect the gate. It is public, and a
# missing read of it must never close the gate while the secret is set — that
# would 403 every route before Turnstile ever had a chance to run. Set it
# anyway: without it the widget never mounts, so nobody can pass the gate.
#
# Unset both in development and the gate is "open", so localhost works with no
# Cloudflare account.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional alias for the site key, read only if the NEXT_PUBLIC_ one is empty.
# It exists because Next and Vercel only ship a variable the source mentions as
# a literal `process.env.NAME`; a bracket lookup is invisible to that pass, and
# production once reported both keys missing and never mounted the widget. Set
# the NEXT_PUBLIC_ name — this is a fallback, not a second thing to configure.
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# ---- the database ----------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres on Supabase holds everything the app remembers between requests:
# the agent's working conversation (1h) and the checkout record (24h) in `kv`,
# the chat and faucet quotas in `quota`, and the archive of signed-in
# conversations in `chat`. Orders are on chain.
#
# Required in production. The quotas fail closed, so without it (or with the
# database down or paused) /api/chat and the faucet answer 503 rather than
# letting unlimited turns through; and a checkout quoted on one lambda must be
# readable from the one that polls it. Locally, leave it unset: an in-process
# Map stands in for `kv` and `quota`, and nothing is archived.
#
# Supabase's free plan pauses a project after about a week without activity,
# and a paused database is a 503 on every chat. Resume it from the dashboard.
#
# Supabase -> Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string. Two of them:
#
#   DATABASE_URL  port 6543, the *transaction* pooler. What the app opens.
#   DIRECT_URL    port 5432, a session connection. `npm run db:migrate` and
#                 `npm run db:invariants` only; the app never reads it.
#
# Add ?sslmode=require to both. lib/db.ts passes `prepare: false`, which the
# pooler needs.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<host>:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
# DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<host>:5432/postgres?sslmode=require

# ---- analytics (optional, public) ------------------------------------------
# Same names as the landing project, so one set of values can be copied onto
# the shopper Vercel project (apps/web) or a different set can be used.
# All three are browser ids. Leave them empty and the shopper loads no
# analytics scripts and records no events. A malformed value is ignored too.
#
# GA4 measurement id, Meta Pixel id, Microsoft Clarity project id.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=

# ---- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Pin the ARS/USD rate instead of reading the live feed, so a demo quotes the
# same number every time. Unset means live. (FX_ARS_PER_USD is no longer read.)
# ARS_PER_USD=1400

# Optional. The agent model. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5. Haiku 4.5 runs (the
# loop switches to a fixed thinking budget for it), but in the one run measured
# here it stopped after the product search without building the cart.
# AGENT_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# Optional. Logs per-hop token usage to the server console.
# AGENT_USAGE=1

# ---- how hard the model thinks (optional) ----------------------------------
# low | medium | high. Defaults to low.
#
# This is the speed knob, not a quality knob in the usual direction. Adaptive
# thinking runs before *every* tool call, and a basket is up to twelve of them,
# so a second of extra deliberation per hop is twelve seconds the shopper
# spends watching "Buscando…". Each hop is a small, well-posed step with the
# tool schemas in front of it, which is not the kind of work that rewards it.
#
# Set medium to restore what shipped before. Move this first if baskets start
# coming back wrong rather than slow.
# AGENT_EFFORT=low
